Provenance of xx-keyboard/glide
==============================

Decoder sources (latinime/)
---------------------------
AOSP LatinIME native decoder, via the owner's xx-keyboard
(ref/xx-keyboard/app/src/main/jni/src), which pins pristine AOSP
LatinIME and carries the owner's own gesture scoring tuning in
suggest/policyimpl/gesture/gesture_scoring_params.cpp.

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; each file keeps its
upstream copyright header. Apache-2.0 code linked into the GPL-3.0
Stevia keyboard is license-compatible (GPL-3.0 whole, Apache-2.0
parts retain their grant).

The copied tree is everything tools/glide-replay's Makefile selects:
all .cpp files under jni/src (there are no com_android_* JNI wrappers
or jni_common files below that directory, so nothing was excluded).
The JNI entry points in jni/com_android_*.cpp were deliberately left
out: xxglide.cpp drives the decoder classes directly with a minimal
host JNIEnv stand-in (same technique as tools/glide-replay/jni_shim.h).

Dictionaries (dicts/)
---------------------
main_en-US.dict and main_en-GB.dict, copied byte-identical from
ref/xx-keyboard/app/src/main/assets/dicts/. AOSP wordlist lineage
(via the HeliBoard aosp-dictionaries collection), Apache-2.0, ver4
binary tries. No license attribute is embedded in the binaries.
